From 0000000000000000000000000000000000000002 Mon Sep 17 00:00:00 2001
From: Copilot <223556219+Copilot@users.noreply.github.com>
Date: Tue, 10 Jun 2026 22:00:00 +0300
Subject: [PATCH 2/2] pci: tegra194: prefer asynchronous probe

Set PROBE_PREFER_ASYNCHRONOUS on the Tegra194/234 PCIe platform driver
so that PCIe link training runs in a separate thread, off the main init
path.

On Lumen the PCIe controller is only needed to reach the NVMe drive.
The NVMe driver already carries PROBE_PREFER_ASYNCHRONOUS (see previous
patch) and the kernel cmdline has "rootwait", so both drivers can train
and enumerate asynchronously while other peripherals also initialise,
shortening the serialised portion of kernel init.

Reference:
https://docs.nvidia.com/jetson/archives/r35.6.2/DeveloperGuide/SD/Kernel/KernelBootTimeOptimization.html#asynchronous-probe

Signed-off-by: Copilot <223556219+Copilot@users.noreply.github.com>
---
 drivers/pci/controller/dwc/pcie-tegra194.c | 5 +++--
 1 file changed, 3 insertions(+), 2 deletions(-)

diff --git a/drivers/pci/controller/dwc/pcie-tegra194.c b/drivers/pci/controller/dwc/pcie-tegra194.c
index ff02af87..00000002 100644
--- a/drivers/pci/controller/dwc/pcie-tegra194.c
+++ b/drivers/pci/controller/dwc/pcie-tegra194.c
@@ -3265,9 +3265,10 @@ static struct platform_driver tegra_pcie_dw_driver = {
 	.probe = tegra_pcie_dw_probe,
 	.remove = tegra_pcie_dw_remove,
 	.shutdown = tegra_pcie_dw_shutdown,
 	.driver = {
-		.name	= "tegra194-pcie",
-		.pm = &tegra_pcie_dw_pm_ops,
-		.of_match_table = tegra_pcie_dw_of_match,
+		.name		= "tegra194-pcie",
+		.pm		= &tegra_pcie_dw_pm_ops,
+		.of_match_table	= tegra_pcie_dw_of_match,
+		.probe_type	= PROBE_PREFER_ASYNCHRONOUS,
 	},
 };
